1712202512525211563 trasjun25.1b_rev2.pdf,28,2317,0,0.0,True,False,False,UNKNOWN,,,False,,,,,Agenda for Discussion with RPCs on 21.07.2025(Monday) | 1. Agenda1: Settlement of RE power station despatched under Tertiary Reserve | Ancillary Services (TRAS) Emergency category. | 1.1. In view of prevailing high frequency in the grid for a significant period a meeting | was held by NLDC/RLDCs on 22.05.2025 with RE developers/associations to | discuss operational issues. A series of measures were discussed including | despatch of RE under TRAS emergency. All RE developers agreed for getting | despatched under TRAS Emergency following which an advisory was issued by,,,
1712202512525211563 trasjun25.1b_rev2.pdf,29,2095,0,0.0,True,False,False,UNKNOWN,,,False,,,,,"2.5.1. This statement shall be done based on the compensation charge declared | by the IPPs. | 2.5.1.1. Those IPPs who have not declared compensation charge, the | statement may be done based on the reference charge rate used for | preparation of the DSM account for that week. | 2.6. IPPs despatched under TRAS from 16.06.25 onwards | 2.6.1. Case-1: Some IPPs provided consent for despatch under TRAS shortfall | and declared their compensation charge. These generators shall be",,,
1712202512525211563 trasjun25.1b_rev2.pdf,30,1819,0,0.0,True,False,False,UNKNOWN,,,False,,,,,"3.1.2. To address these issues, it is proposed to follow the practice prevailing at | NRPC where any difference arising due to past period account revision is | incorporated in the upcoming weekly statement. The statements are | prepared separately and in consolidated manners also. All entities are paying | or receiving based on the consolidated statement which factors all past | revisions. | 3.2. Clarification on reciprocal interest liability from pool in DSM, Ancillary Services, | SCUC, reactive and congestion accounts:",,,
1712202512525211563 trasjun25.1b_rev2.pdf,31,2938,0,0.0,True,False,False,UNKNOWN,,,False,,,,,"Minutes of the Meeting dated 21.07.2025 with RPCs on Accounting | Settlement of TRAS-Emergency and Comments on the draft procedure | for National Pool Account | An online meeting was convened on 21-07-2025 by NLDC with participation from all RPCs, | RLDCs and NLDC to deliberate on issues related to the accounting and settlement of despatch | made under TRAS emergency as well as the comments received on draft procedure on National | Pool Account prepared by NLDC as per the mandate under CERC DSM Regulations 2024. List of | participants is enclosed as Annexure-1.",,,
1712202512525211563 trasjun25.1b_rev2.pdf,32,3044,0,0.0,True,False,False,UNKNOWN,,,False,,,,,"NLDC also informed that some of the RE plants have conveyed their consents in compliance of | the RoP directions from CERC in the above petition (diary no. 292/2025). | Decision: It was decided that NLDC will share with RPCs the details of plant who have given | consent for participation in Ancillary Services – TRAS Shortfall and/or Emergency Category with | the compensation rates. | RPCs will publish the accounts accordingly. For the RE plants who have not yet given consent, | the settlement would be done considering zero compensation charge. NLDC will share with all | RPCs the details of plants who have given consent for participation in Ancillary Services – under",,,
1712202512525211563 trasjun25.1b_rev2.pdf,33,2725,0,0.0,True,False,False,UNKNOWN,,,False,,,,,Same rate shall be used by NLDC while preparing the merit order stack for despatch | of theses generating station under TRAS-Emergency. | (vi) NLDC shall publish all the rates on Grid-India's website before 16th of every month. | The same rate shall be considered for preparing merit order despatch by NLDC and | publication of the statement by RPCs. | Agenda 3: Comments from RPCs and Beneficiaries on the Draft procedure prepared | by NLDC for implementation of National Pool Account | 3.1: Stakeholders highlighted that issuance of revised and regular weekly statements in the,,,
1712202512525211563 trasjun25.1b_rev2.pdf,34,2030,0,0.0,True,False,False,UNKNOWN,,,False,,,,,"and ancillary pool account transfer of amounts to PSDF. Also, it would streamline the | issuance of DSM deficit recovery billing and timely computation of SCED benefits. | The issue was explained by NLDC highlighting the need for timely publication of heat rate | compensation statement by all RPCs in a harmonized manner so as to have a realistic picture of | pool surplus/deficit status at any point of time. | All RPCs appreciated the concern and agreed to publish the compensation Heat Rate | compensation statement (SCUC & SCED) for previous month by 20th day of next month. | Agenda 4: Additional items:",,,
